<title>BELGIUM: GOLF-VOLVO MASTERS STAYS IN SPAIN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-VOLVO MASTERS STAYS IN SPAIN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Volvo Masters golf championship, played for the last nine years at Valderrama, will stay in Spain next year when it moves to the Jack Nicklaus-designed Montecastillo course in Jerez, the sponsors announced on Friday.</p>
<p>The final event in the European Tour  season, won this year by Mark McNulty of Zimbabwe, is being moved because Valderrama is staging the Ryder Cup in September.</p>
<p>Next year's event will be held from October 30 to November 2.</p>
</text>
